Note: this has been superseded and is retained for historical reasons.


Assassin Bear	Teacher Bear's [[:Category:Black Enemies|Black]] variant. He possesses extreme speed, DPS and range yet has less money drop and health, so low that even the [[Cat Cannon]] can take him out when not buffed to an extent. Often used in gimmicky stages as a makeshift time limit, as he mostly guarantees the player's loss if heavily buffed/spammed or if the Cannon isn't prepared.
Shy Boy	A [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]/[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] variant of The Face. Attacks and moves much faster, but has much less health and deals less damage per attack. Has well-rounded stats when buffed and can destroy your front lines considerably fast if not stalled correctly.
Doge Dark	A [[:Category:Black Enemies|Black]] variant of Doge with superior overall stats and more knockbacks. Drops a good amount of money for how easily it is killed.
Metal Hippoe	Hippoe's [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] variant, and the first Metal enemy encountered in the game. In terms of stats it is one of the weakest, but its metal trait allows it to take a beating from anything that isn't a [[Critical Hit]].
St. Pigge the 2nd	A much bigger version of Pigge which usually replaces Pigge in [[Legend Stages#Stories of Legend|Stories of Legend]]. Attacks faster, has high health and double the knockback count.
J.K Bun Bun	Teacher Bun Bun's [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] variant. Slightly smaller in aesthetic size. Stats are only slightly more than a 400% Teacher Bun Bun, but he has half the number of knockbacks.
Bun Bun Black	Teacher Bun Bun's [[:Category:Black Enemies|Black]] variant. Bigger in aesthetic size. Superior health, but has less speed and attack power than a 400% Bun Bun, as well as the same number of knockbacks.
Gory Black	Gory's first [[:Category:Black Enemies|Black]] enemy variant. He has much more health, knockbacks and damage, and twice the movement speed.
Shadow Boxer K	Kang Roo's [[:Category:Black Enemies|Black]] variant, with much higher stats, Area Attack, more knockbacks and a faster attack rate.
Director Kurosawah	Dark Emperor Nyandam's [[:Category:Black Enemies|Black]] variant, with higher attack damage and range. More glass cannon-oriented, generally having lower health than the buffed Dark Emperor Nyandams encountered around the same point in the game.
Super Metal Hippoe	A much faster and stronger version of Metal Hippoe that only appears in [[The Aku Realms]] and [[Legend Stages]]. He has a whopping 16 knockbacks and high health for a metal enemy, with a 100% chance to knockback cats on hit.
Type 10	A Doge in a [[wikipedia:Type 10|Type 10]] tank. Has the [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] trait, with extremely low stats overall. Appears in [[Unseen in 2019]].
Metal One Horn	A [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] variant of One Horn. Has extreme DPS and takes only one damage from non-[[Critical Hit|Critical]] attacks, but has very low health, is knocked back twice and is only slightly faster.
Teacher Cybear	[[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] variant of Teacher Bear. Has single-target attacks with extreme damage, range and attack rate.
CyberFace	A [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] variant of The Face. Has very low health but compensates for it with extreme damage, high speed, Base Destroyer and an incredibly powerful [[Wave Attack]] that can one-shot almost every unit in the game, with a chance to knockback [[Cat Units]] if they aren't killed by the Wave or initial hit. However, it dies to any [[Critical Hit]] due to its terrible health.
Sir Metal Seal	Sir Seal's [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] variant, with a higher attack rate, damage and health, as well as having the usual attributes of a Metal enemy.
Princess Head	A variant of The Face with [[Kerihime (Special Cat)|Princess Punt]] hair. 1/3 as fast as [[Doge Dark]]. Attacks about as fast as Shy Boy and does 2,400 damage at 100% strength magnification.
Chief Peng	An event-exclusive enemy introduced in [[Loving Labour (Monthly Event)|Loving Labor]].
Dark Emperor Santa	A Christmas version of Nyandam with less health but more attack power, no delay between attacks and the ability to [[freeze]] the movement of [[Cat Units]]. Traited as [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]/[[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]].
Lione Hippoe	An enemy introduced in the [[Happy New Year? (Monthly Event)|Happy New Year?]] event (January event).
Lucky Sloth	An enemy from the [[Ritual Happiness (Monthly Event)|Ritual Happiness]] event. It has similar stats, lower range, a faster attack rate and a 20% chance to knockback cats.
Bears Be Bare	A group of bears sitting together on a bleacher introduced in the [[Bears be Bare (Monthly Event)|Bears be Bare]] event.
White Cyclone	Very similar to Red Cyclone in terms of stats, but with more knockbacks. Its lack of a secondary trait may make it slightly harder to counter than the previous Cyclones. It appears in [[Attack on W-Cyclone (Expert)|Peerless]] and [[Peerless Too]].
Black Cyclone	Its damage per hit is quite low, but its 20% chance to [[Special Abilities#Knockback|knockback]] Cat Units somewhat makes up for it. However, Black Cyclone itself gets knocked back up to 10 times. It appears in [[Attack on B-Cyclone (Expert)|Heaven of Darkness]] and [[NEO Darkness Heaven]]
Metal Cyclone	It has the highest health of any [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemy, making [[Critical Hit]]s a necessity to defeat it. Moves very slowly, and has as many knockbacks as the Black Cyclone. It appears in [[Attack on Titanium (Insane)|Sweet Irony]] and [[Bitter Irony]].
Teacher A	An event enemy first seen in the [[Teacher! It's Spring! (Monthly Event)|Teacher! It's Spring!]] monthly event. Can [[Special Abilities#Slow|slow]] down Cat Units, but has 100 less range.
Samurai Doggy	A Red-Black hybrid variant consisting of [[Doge Dark]] riding a One Horn. First appears in [[Love is Sickness (Monthly Event)|Love is Sickness]]. They're much faster with greater DPS, attack rate, and 100% chance to knockback cats, as well as two knockbacks instead of one.
Gory Groom	A bigger variant of Gory Black. He is one of the strongest Gory variants in terms of stats, but is also the slowest. First appears in [[The Forbidden Bride (Monthly Event)|The Forbidden Bride]].
Sunny Celeboodle	Celeboodle takes her [[Never Summer! (Monthly Event)|summer]] vacation! She has much higher HP as well as Area Attack and longer range. The downside of these buffs are that she has lower base damage and usually spawns alone.
Bearkini	A much faster variant of Teacher Bear wearing a bikini. First encountered in the [[Never Summer! (Monthly Event)|Never Summer!]] event.
Lord Enma	This [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] enemy first seen in [[Ghostly Houseguests (Monthly Event)|Ghostly Houseguests]] is a combination of [[Doge]] and Le'boin.
Dashing Face	A [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] variant of The Face with feet and thus no Floating trait. Considerably faster than The Face (has half of Shy Boy's speed) and has a much faster attack speed, but has about half of The Face's health.
Ghost Doge	A [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] variant of Doge introduced in the [[Ghostly Houseguests (Monthly Event)|Ghostly Houseguests]] event.
Ghost Snache	A [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] variant of Snache introduced in the [[Ghostly Houseguests (Monthly Event)|Ghostly Houseguests]] event. Has double the health and damage of Snache.
Ghost Baa Baa	Baa Baa's [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] variant, with twice as much health and attack power. First introduced in [[Ghostly Houseguests (Monthly Event)|Ghostly Houseguests]], it also appears in [[The Haunted 1LDK]].
Fireworks Guys (High-Yield)	A harmless pair of stick figures with a firework cannon. Can be found in many events.
Fireworks Guys (Low-Yield)	The same as Firework Guys 1, but with double the range.
Mighty Gui Zuli	A buffer variant of Teacher Bear introduced in the [[Old Guys About Town (Monthly Event)|Old Guys About Town]] event. This enemy has a higher overall DPS with its increased attack rate and damage while having only three knockbacks.
Hermit Peng	An event-exclusive enemy introduced in [[Old Guys About Town (Monthly Event)|Old Guys About Town]].
Master Da Xun	An enemy introduced in [[Old Guys About Town (Monthly Event)|Old Guys About Town]]. He has strong attack power and requires multiple knockbacks to kill.
Pigge Back	3 [[Doge]]s holding up a Pigge. Has double the attack speed and range of Pigge, and higher health. First appears in the [[Autumn = Sports Day! (Monthly Event)|Autumn = Sports Day!]] event.
Divine Cyclone	The first non-[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] Cyclone; units such as [[Stilts Cat (Rare Cat)|Stilts Cat]], [[Cat Toaster (Super Rare Cat)|Cat Toaster]] and [[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Juliet Cat]] are needed to keep it at bay. It appears in [[Oncoming Maelstrom (Expert)|Wrath of Heaven]] and [[Wrath of the Divine]].
Heavenly Hippoe	Hippoe's [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] variant. He has high stats and rapid attacks.
Gabriel	Gabriel is Doge's [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] variant. Behaves similarly to Doge Dark, but with shorter range, Area Attack, faster movement and more knockbacks.
Angelic Gory	Gory's [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] variant, with even more health, damage and speed than Gory Black.
Angel Fanboy	A weak [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemy that exists to remind the player that [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating]] abilities won't work on [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]]. Holds a sign saying, "<span style{{=
Wall Doge	[[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cat]]'s Doge counterpart. Has much more health and damage, with Area Attack and lower speed.
Ginger Snache	A [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] variant of Snache commonly seen in Legend Stages. It has much higher health, movement speed, attack power and knockbacks.
Birthday Cake	A birthday cake carried by 3 Doges. Has moderate HP and the Metal trait with just 1 attack power. Appears in Memorial Events.
Dark Otter	A [[:Category:Black Enemies|Black]] variant of Otta-smack-u, with much higher overall stats, but slower movement speed and 2 knockbacks.
Sunrise Doge	A stationary Metal enemy with the face of a Doge. Has incredible range and always freezes cats for a short time, but does almost no damage. Appears in [[Year's First Dawn]].
Trolly Blogger	An enemy commonly seen in later [[Legend Stages]]. Moves faster, with high range for a peon, rapid area attacks and 15% chance to cause knockback.
Metal Doge	A Metal variant of Doge sporting far superior attack rate, movement speed and area damage, along the Metal trait & low health.
Li'l Nyandam	A smaller Red variant that has higher range, a faster attack rate and greater damage. Appears at the end of [[Stories of Legend]] sub-chapter 23, [[Dead End Night]], from which he can be unlocked as a [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Cat Unit]].
Le'noir	A [[:Category:Black Enemies|Black]] variant of Le'boin. Has far higher health and damage, and slightly more range.
Ayumi Manbosaki	A [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] variant of Sunfish Jones that only appears in the [[Survive! Mola Mola! Collaboration Event]]. Much weaker overall, but has 1 knockback instead of 4, and receives massive buffs in later stages.
Marching Kory	A Traitless enemy introduced in the [[Cats in Love#Sweetest Sorrow|Sweetest Sorrow]] event. He has improved health, damage, speed and attack rate, but is the only variant to lack wave attacks.
Shibalien	[[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] version of Doge. Slightly faster in terms of speed, with much higher strength and slightly improved attack rate than Doge.
Kroxo	The [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] variant of Croco. He is slower, has 4 knockbacks and far higher stats.
Hyppoh	[[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] version of Hippoe. She is much stronger and has longer range than Hippoe, though not as dangerous as Heavenly Hippoe.
Imperator Sael	Sir Seal's [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] variant. He is much stronger and can slow the movement of Cat Units. However, he is slower in terms of speed and attack speed, and has more knockbacks.
Maawth	[[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] version of Mooth. He is stronger, has longer range (370) and 30% chance to [[Special Abilities#Freeze|freeze]] Cat Units for 2 seconds.
I.M. Phace	An [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]]/[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] version of The Face. Much faster and has a chance to freeze Cat Units. To add insult to injury, he has longer range, making him very hard for [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cat]] and [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Psychocat]] to survive long against him. He gets knocked back twice as much as The Face.
Ursamajor	An [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] variant of Teacher Bear. Possesses superior overall stats and strengthens by 50% at 50% health.
Nimoy Bore	[[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] variant of Bore. Inferior speed, attack rate and base health but has a 50% chance to knockback [[Cat Units]].
Elizabeth the LVIth	[[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] variant of St. Pigge the 2nd. She has much higher health, and 100% chance to create a level 3 [[Wave Attack]].
Cosmic Cyclone	It has significantly longer range than most Cyclones, though not enough to reach [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necro-Dancer Cat]] or [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Psychocat]]. It strengthens by 200% at 30% health. It appears in [[Black Hole Rising (Insane)|Dimension of Despair]] and [[Dimension of Delirium]].
Galactic Overseer Nyandam	An [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] version of Nyandam that has a chance to [[slow]] Cat Units. He also has longer range and more damage.
Scissoroo	Kang Roo's [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] variant, with Area Attack, longer range, no multi-hit and a chance to knockback cats.
Cyberhorn	An [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] variant of One Horn, with much more health and damage.
Mistress Celeboodle	An [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] variant of Celeboodle. She has a higher money drop and deals much more damage, while strengthening by 100% at 75% health.
Professor A.	A [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] variant of Master A. He has even longer range, higher damage and very high health. Just like Teacher A., he has a chance to slow your cats.
Pumpkin Doge	A Doge hiding inside a pumpkin, introduced in [[HALLOWEEN EVENT#All Hallows Road|All Hallows Road]].
Count Owlbrow	A larger variant introduced in [[HALLOWEEN EVENT#All Hallows Road|All Hallows Road]]. Can knockback [[Cat Units]] and has more health, damage and range, but moves slower and has an additional knockback.
Vlad de Sable	A weaker variant of Pigeon de Sable first seen in the [[HALLOWEEN EVENT#All Hallows Road|All Hallows Road]] event. It moves slower, has less health, damage and range, has an extra knockback, and unlike its avian counterpart, it can't release Wave Attacks.
Berserkory	A [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] variant of Kory. He is much more durable, with only one knockback and level 12 wave attacks, but doesn't have Base Destroyer.
Alpacky	Camelle's [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] variant. She has more health but attacks slower with less damage. She strengthens by 900% at 1% health and has 100% chance to survive a lethal strike.
Elder Sloth	An [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] variant of THE SLOTH, with increased speed, range, and 100% chance to knockback Cat Units.
Bun Bun Symbiote	Teacher Bun Bun's [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] variant. Slightly bigger than Bun Bun Black. Has superior health & attack power, with half as many knockbacks and a 5% chance to create a Lv. 1 [[Wave Attack|Wave]].
Christmas D.	A [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] variant of Rain D. that first appears in [[MERRY CATMAS!#Jolly St. Nick|Jolly St. Nick]]. It has higher stats and a 30% chance to knockback cats.
Cruel Angel Clionel	An [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] variant of Cli-One that has more health and damage, fewer knockbacks, faster attacks and the ability to [[Special Abilities#Slow|slow]] Cats, but has a blind spot.
The Perfect Cyclone	Has extreme range and very high DPS compared to other enemies with similar range. Its weakness is that it can't hit units that are too close to it, making it vulnerable to tanks with enough health and few enough knockbacks to enter its blind spot, like [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]], [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Titan Cat]] and [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Kotatsu Cat]]. It appears in [[Oncoming Storm (Insane)|Red Sky at Morning]] and [[Red Sky at Night]].
Mr. Angel	An [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] variant of Trolly Blogger. Moves even faster than Trolly Blogger, gets knocked back more times and has a chance to weaken cats.
Boraphim	[[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] variant of Bore. Much stronger and moves significantly faster, but has 5 knockbacks as opposed to the usual 2 on most others.
Ritual Drum Doge	A "Macho Doge" on a [[wikipedia:Taiko|Taiko drum]], it is a stationary enemy, has extremely long range, high health and a 100% chance to freeze cats, but deals minimal damage. Similar to Angry Sun, appears in [[Summer in Catland|Summer Diary]].
Festive Otter	An event variant of Otta-smack-u first seen in [[Summer Break Cats|Summer Diary]]. Deals higher damage and has 4x more HP with 2 knockbacks, as well as a 50% chance to knockback cats.
Hannya	A red variant that moves slowly, but with exceptional range, damage, health, and 100% chance to weaken cats to 25% for 5 seconds. Introduced as the boss of [[Realm of Carnage (Deadly)|River Styx]].
Package Doge	A Doge-faced cardboard box used for delivery. Stationary, with the Metal trait and extremely low health and attack power. Appears in [[Sender Unknown]].
Li'l Bun Bun	A much smaller variant of Teacher Bun Bun. Has lower health, attack power and range, but is much faster, gets knocked back half as many times, drops less money and appears in swarms along with extreme buffs.
Razorback	[[:Category:Black Enemies|Black]] variant of Bore. Has extremely high health, speed and DPS, while strengthening by 50% at 50% health.
Vendor El	A [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] variant of Chickful A, with quicker attack speed but less range, damage and health. It also has a chance to [[Special Abilities#Weaken|weaken]] Cats instead of Chickful A's [[Special Abilities#Freeze|freeze]].
Zoge	The [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant of Doge. Far stronger, has fewer knock backs, can burrow under cats and revives once with 50% HP.
Znache	A [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant of Snache. Revives once, stats are increased greatly, and has Area Attacks.
Zomboe	[[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant of Hippoe. It has 40x as much health and damage as Hippoe, slightly longer range, and 30% chance to slow cats for 4 seconds. Like most Zombies, it can also burrow under cats and revive once with 50% HP.
Zigge	[[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant of Pigge. Has higher health and damage, is a little bit faster, and can knockback units. Like most Zombies, she can burrow past cats and revive once with 50% HP.
Zackie Peng	A [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant of Jackie Peng, with much more health and attack power. Like most Zombies, he can burrow past cats and revives once with 50% HP.
Zory	Gory's [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant. He has much more health and damage, and also less knockbacks. Can burrow under cats once, and revives with full health after being killed.
Zir Zeal	Sir Seal's [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant. He has much higher stats in all areas than Sir Seal, combined with a Freeze ability and the regular [[Special Abilities#Burrow|Zombie]]-[[Special Abilities#Revive|type]] abilities.
Zang Roo	Kang Roo's [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant, with much higher stats and Area Attack. Burrows under cats and revives once with 100% HP.
Zroco	The [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant of Croco. It retains his singular knockback and deals much more damage, with a 30% chance to weaken cat units by 50% for 5 seconds. It also pushes with a short-ranged burrow and revives once after a long delay.
Zyclone	A Cyclone that can revive with 100% health an unlimited number of times. To win against it, the player will need to defeat it with [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killers]] or sneak units past it before it can revive. Unlike most [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]], it can't burrow past Cat Units. It appears in [[Unholy Tempest (Insane)|The Rolling Dead]] and [[The Dead Keep Rolling]].
Le'mammoth	An event variant of Le'boin introduced in the [[Cats in the Snow]] event, with the ability to create [[Wave Attack]]s. Also appears in [[Zero Legends]].
Ice Doge	An ice-themed variant of Wall Doge first seen in [[Cats in the Snow]]. Has more health, along with very slightly increased attack power and range.
Coffin Zoge	Wall Doge's [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant. It has higher health, slightly increased damage and range, and can [[Special Abilities#Revive|revive]] with 100% HP an unlimited number of times. Unlike most other Zombies, it cannot [[Special Abilities#Burrow|burrow]] past your cats.
Zamelle	Camelle's [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant. Don't be fooled by the abnormal only-slightly-higher HP, because while she does not burrow, she can revive infinitely, always appears above 200% and has much higher attack power at a reduced attack rate.
Easter Duche	A much larger variant of Duche introduced in the [[Cats Abloom!|Spring Sprang Sprung]] event, with higher stats.
Easter B.B.Bunny	A [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] variant of B.B.Bunny that first appears in [[Cats Abloom!|Spring Sprang Sprung]].
Golden Doge	A golden variant of Doge wearing a top hat and monocle. Drops a large amount of money when killed. Introduced in [[GOLD RUSH#The Midas Touch|The Midas Touch]].
Gold Hippoe	An enemy that originates in [[GOLD RUSH#The Midas Touch|The Midas Touch]], with increased health, damage, range, and movement speed. He can freeze cats, and drops a lot of money when killed.
Pure Gold R.Ost	A [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemy introduced in the [[GOLD RUSH#The Midas Touch|Golden Week]] event. It has the usual Metal ability of only taking 1 damage except for Critical Hits, but it has much lower stats all across the board and cannot perform Critical Hits itself.
Cala Maria	An [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] variant of Calamary that has much higher health, damage and a multi-hit attack, but in return has Single Target and loses her weaken ability.
Gudetama Plate	A weak enemy found in the [[Gudetama Collaboration Event]].
Gudegude à la mode	Another Gudetama Collaboration Event enemy, it has a 50% chance to knockback Cat Units.
Nisetama Army	A fast-moving enemy from the Gudetama Collaboration Event with decent health and range.
Gary Gory	An enemy from the [[Summer Break Cats|Summer Lesson]] event, he has moderate health and high damage, more range, faster attacks and faster movement than the original Gory. He also strengthens by 100% at 50% health.
Metal Snache	A [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] variant of Snache that appears in [[Silver Week]] and the [[Heavenly Tower]]. Very similar to [[Metal Doge]], but trades damage and Area Attack for almost double health.
THE METAL SLOTH	A [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] variant of THE SLOTH. Has a faster attack rate and movement speed, but lower range and damage.
Shibalien Elite	The Starred Alien variant of Doge. He has massively increased stats, slightly higher speed and a chance of Warping cats backward.
Star Peng	A [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Alien]] variant of Jackie Peng. It has significantly increased stats and a 100% chance to warp cats backward.
General GreGory	Gory's [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Alien]] variant. He has a weak [[Barrier]] with a breaking point of 6,000. He also has more knockbacks, health, damage and range.
Le'Solar	A [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Alien]] variant of Le'boin. She has a 40,000 HP [[Barrier]] as well as increased health, damage and attack speed.
Project A	A [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Alien]] variant of Master A. He has a chance to [[Special Abilities#Warp|warp]] cats backward with each hit, but is weaker in terms of stats.
Corporal Weyland	A [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Alien]] variant of Mr. Mole. He has lower health, damage and range, along with a  2,500 HP [[Barrier|barrier]] and 30% chance to [[warp]] your cats backwards.
Spacefish Jones	A [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Alien]]/[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] variant of Sunfish Jones. Generally deals much higher damage than Sunfish Jones, but has much less health. It also has a [[Barrier]] with a breaking point of 12,000.
Youcan	Two Can's [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]]/[[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Alien]] variant. Has slightly longer Wave Attacks, [[Special Abilities#Area Attack|Area Attack]], and a [[Barrier]] with a breaking point of 266,000.
Super Cosmic Cyclone	This Cyclone is a [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Alien]], which means its difficulty will vary depending on one's [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]]. Its damage is fairly low no matter how many Treasures the player has, but it Warps cats back with every attack. It has even longer range than Cosmic Cyclone: enough to hit [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Surfer Cat]], but still not enough to reach [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Psychocat]]. It appears in [[The Wormhole Opens (Deadly)|The 2nd Dimension]] and [[The 3rd Dimension]].
Winged Pigge	[[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] variant of St. Pigge the 2nd. Has much higher health and damage and an [[Special Abilities|Omni Strike]] that reaches 340 range, moves faster, and weakens cats by 90% for 5 seconds.
Hackey	A [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] fire-breathing variant of Tackey. He has higher health, greater effective range and deals extreme damage, but has a slower attack rate and a massive blind spot.
UltraBaaBaa	Baa Baa's [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Alien]] variant, with increased movement speed and higher damage, but more importantly, a [[Barrier]] with 266,000 HP. Still has single-target attacks.
Pigge Victorious	A variant of Pigge Back, the Pigge is now flipped upwards and she has a school jacket. Has even higher range and attack speed, with much higher stats. First appears in the [[FINALS WEEK#Go Go Graduates!|Go Go Graduates!]] event.
Bang-Bang	An enemy introduced in [[FINALS WEEK#Go Go Graduates!|Go Go Graduates!]], with 3x more health, longer range and higher damage.
Corrupted Moneko	Corrupted Moneko has identical stats to Crazed Moneko, the only difference being that Corrupted Moneko appears at 100% strength magnification while Crazed Moneko only appears at 12% and 50%.
Glowstick Guys	A much weaker variant of Those Guys wearing neon colored bandanas and holding penlights with the same color. Found in the [[Crazed Moneko]] and [[Hatsune Miku Collaboration Event#Hatsune Miku|Hatsune Miku]] Stages.
Moe Uzumasa & Doge	Chibi version of [[Get On! Kyoto City Subway Collaboration Event|Get On! Kyoto City Subway]] mascot Moe Uzumasa with a Doge by her side. Has Long Distance attacks.
Saki Matsuga & Doge	Chibi version of Get On! Kyoto City Subway mascot Saki Matsuga with a Doge by her side. The strongest and fastest enemy in the collab, with the ability to weaken groups of cats for 5 seconds.
Misa Ono & Doge	Chibi version of Get On! Kyoto City Subway mascot Misa Ono with a Doge by her side. Sports exceptional range and can weaken cats for a few seconds, but deals mediocre damage.
Mecha-Bun	The final boss of [[Stories of Legend]], a visually mechanical variant of Teacher Bun Bun piloted by a [[Doge]]. Has a gigantic amount of health and damage, a faster attack rate, and piercing Omni Strikes. Despite having Mecha in its name, it's not considered a [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemy and keeps the Floating trait. After clearing its debut stage, [[Eldritch Forces]], Mecha-Bun is unlocked as a [[Mecha-Bun (Special Cat)|Legend Cat]].
Relic Bun-Bun	Mecha-Bun's [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] variant. Attacks even faster, gets knocked back half as many times, has even longer reach, deals half as much damage, moves slower, and is guaranteed to [[Special Abilities#Curse|curse]] Cat Units for 10 seconds. Once its debut stage ([[An Ancient Curse]]) is cleared, Mecha-Bun's True Form becomes available. Unlike most other variants, Relic Bun-Bun is '''not''' a Floating enemy.
Relic Doge	Doge's [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] variant. It has massively increased stats, improved speed, rapid area attacks and a chance to inflict the Curse effect.
Gude-Doge Machine	A Doge piloting a [[Gude-Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Gude-Cat Machine]]. Appears in the Gudetama Collaboration Event.
Gorilliam	Gory Groom's Alien variant, with less knockbacks, higher health and range, and a high chance of warping cats back by 500. First appears in [[Forbidden Bride Pt II (Monthly Event)|Forbidden Bride Pt II]].
Sir Rel	A [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] variant of Squire Rel, with insane DPS, much higher health and speed, five knockbacks and a lower money drop. Like most Relics, he has a guaranteed chance to [[Curse]] Cat Units.
Oldhorn	A [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] variant of One Horn, with a ridiculous amount of health, DPS, and the ability to [[Special Abilities#Curse|Curse]] Cat Units but still retains pitiful range and movement speed.
Othom	[[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] version of Mooth. Far stronger, with an Omni Strike hitting up to 440 range and a guaranteed chance to [[Special Abilities#Curse|curse]] Cat Units for 2 seconds, but has relatively low damage for a Relic.
Selena	Sunny Celeboodle's [[:Category:Black Enemies|Black]] variant. She attacks quicker and is considerably stronger, with [[knockback]] and [[slow]] abilities, but has much shorter range.
Kid Tappa	The [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Alien]] version of Dolphina. Deals very low damage and has short reach with a very long backswing, but has high health and a Barrier with a breaking point of 15,000, primarily serving as a frontline tank for other threats to advance.
Ribbo	A [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Alien]] variant of Croakley. Has lower range, extremely low health, a [[Barrier]] with a breaking point of 65,000, and [[Warp]]s back cats instead of slowing them down.
Loris	A [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] enemy that combines LeMurr's survivability with [[Tackey]]'s constant Long Distance attacks. Instead of applying weaken, he curses units for 5 seconds, effectively perma-cursing them if they can't enter his blind spot.
Heavenly Le'saint	An [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] variant of Lord Enma. He has a faster attack rate and gets stronger at 50% HP, but has the shortest range of all Le'boin variants.
The Red Malice	A [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] variant of Mighty Gui Zuli. Compared to Zuli, The Red Malice is much faster and attacks more often, but has more knockbacks, less damage, less range, and a 100% chance to knockback Cat Units on hit.
Lowkey	A [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]]/[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] variant of The Face, with far more range, rapid attacks, 100% chance to curse cats for 10 seconds and only one knockback.
M. Ost	The [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] variant of R.Ost, with even higher health, damage, range and speed, but double the knockbacks. Instead of doing Critical Hits, M. Ost has a 100% chance to [[curse]], [[knockback]] and [[slow]] cats with each hit.
Dead Donny Dash	A [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant of Dashing Face. Has Long Distance attacks, burrows 750 towards the [[Cat Base]] and revives once at 100% HP.
CTO Seal	A [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] variant of Otta-smack-u introduced in the [[Worker's Revolution (Monthly Event)|Worker's Revolution]] event. It has a 100% chance of [[freeze|freezing]] cats and has much higher range (380), allowing it to outrange [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Salon]] and [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cat]].
Cadaver Bear	[[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant of Teacher Bear. Attacks much faster, can burrow under Cat Units and revives once with 100% HP.
Dread Bore	[[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant of Bore. Stats are similar to Bore's except for speed, which is slightly lower than Boraphim's. It has a long burrow distance among Zombies, and revives once with 50% HP.
Satan Claus	Another Alien variant, with health on par with normal Nyandam variants but much less range, a significantly shorter delay between attacks, faster movement speed and the ability to [[warp]] back Cat Units.
Sister Lione	An enemy first seen in [[Another New Year (Monthly Event)|Another New Year]]. Has more health and range, plus a guaranteed chance to [[Special Abilities#Weaken|weaken]] Cat Units' attack power to 50%, with many knockbacks, but slower.
Lucky Dags	A [[:Category:Black Enemies|Black]] variant introduced in [[Ritual Confusion (Monthly Event)|Ritual Confusion]], with strong yet single-target attacks.
Primeval Cyclone	This Cyclone can only be fought after clearing [[Stories of Legend]]. It has the highest health and movement speed of any Cyclone, and increases its attack power by 200% after reaching 50% health. Given that it is a [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] enemy, there are very few units that can reliably stall it other than [[Talents|Talented]] [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Rodeo Cat]], Talented [[Fortune Teller Cat (Rare Cat)|Doctor Cat]] and [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Freshman Cat Jobs]]. It appears in [[Charybdis' Mouth (Merciless)|Typhoon Nemo]] and [[Typhoon Nihil]].
Li'l Bore	A much smaller and weaker variant of Bore found in [[Year's First Dawn|You Nears! 2019]], [[Most Appearances 2020]] and [[Infernal Tower]] Can be easily defeated.
Bears Be Back	A [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]/[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]]/[[:Category:Black Enemies|Black]]/[[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]]/[[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]]/[[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant of Bears Be Bare introduced in the [[Bears Be Back (Monthly Event)|Bears Be Back]] event. Compared to Bears Be Bare, they have the same health, higher range, slower movement speed, a multi-hit attack, and the ability to afflict cats with a wide range of debuffs. They have the most traits out of every enemy in the game.
Ms. Madonna	First seen in the [[Spring for Sensei (Monthly Event)|Spring for Sensei]] event. Attacks less often, but has a 100% chance to knockback cats and create a Lv.3 [[Wave Attack]].
Mesocosmocyclone	A very strong [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Alien]] peon that warps Cat Units ''forward'' with every hit, while also having fast movement speed, short range and non-stop attacks. As such, it can push at terrifying speeds when not met with crowd-controllers or [[:Category:Cats with Warp Immunity|Cats with Warp Immunity]]. It appears in [[Cats of the Cosmos]] Chapter 3 and [[Legend Stages#Uncanny Legends|Uncanny Legends]].
Axoloty	Big Sal's [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Alien]] variant. It has a [[Barrier]] with 10k HP and can create lethal Lv.10 [[Wave Attack]]s from a distance, but has a backswing lasting over 4 minutes. This backswing is the only delay between attacks that it has, so each of its 5 knockbacks gives it another chance to strike.
Haterbaa 2.0	Baa Baa's [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] variant, with less health but much more damage. Luckily, it still only has single-target attacks. First appears in [[Lovesick Again (Monthly Event)|Lovesick Again]].
Zuche	A [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant of Duche, first appearing in [[Into the Future]] Chapter 2's [[Zombie Outbreaks]]. He is a glass cannon with abnormally low health, high speed and damage and the [[Special Abilities#Burrow|burrow]] and [[Special Abilities#Revive|revive]] abilities.
The Thrillerz	A [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant of Those Guys, introduced in [[Into the Future]] Chapter 2's [[Zombie Outbreaks]]. They have higher health, damage and speed, revive once with 100% health and can burrow twice.
Shakurel Doge	A slightly stronger version of Doge that appears in the [[Shakurel Planet Collaboration Event]].
Shakurel Gory	A variant of Gory from the [[Shakurel Planet Collaboration Event]]. Has double the health and attack power but isn't too difficult otherwise.
Shakurel Face	A variant of The Face that only appears in the [[Shakurel Planet Collaboration Event|Shakurel Planet]] stages. Has quadruple the health and damage of a normal Face.
Li'l Cake Doge	An even weaker version of Birthday Cake that appears during [[CAT DAY|Meow Meow Day]].
Puffsley's Comet	Mr. Puffington's [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] variant, introduced as the boss of the [[:Category:Advent Stages|Advent Stage]] [[Puffer Planet (Merciless)|Blue Impact]]. He has a larger area of effect and knocks units back instead of Cursing them.
Black Okame	A [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]/[[:Category:Black Enemies|Black]] variant of Hannya, with freeze immunity, much more HP, only one knockback, less damage and faster attacks, as well as 100% chance to knockback cats. Though its standing range is subpar, its Omni Strike gives it extreme reach.
Heavenly Herald Papuu	Daboo of the Dead's [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] variant. She has less health, attack power and range, but has only one knockback, a faster attack rate, a further Omni Strike and triple damage when her HP is lowered. Instead of slowing cats, she deals 40% Toxic damage, killing units without Toxic immunity/resistance in up to three hits.
Queen Mother V	Queen B's [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]]/[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] variant. Deals more damage and, instead of slowing cats, she [[curse]]s them for almost ''2 minutes'', but attacks more slowly and has more knockbacks.
Rat Doge	A Doge wearing a rat costume. Appears in Year's First Dawn and [[Joy & Prosperity|Lunar New Year]] 2020.
Urs & Fenrir	Ururun Wolf's [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] variant, with more health and attack power, a big [[Special Abilities#Omni Strike|Omni Strike]], weaken and curse but less movement speed, range and knockbacks.
Croconator	The [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] variant of Croco. Although he does more damage, he attacks slower, and has extremely low health for a metal.
Baron Seal	A [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] variant of Sir Seal appearing in [[Baron Seal Strikes]]. This seal appears with a large variety of buffs in the stages he appears in, and can also weaken and freeze Cat Units.
MikuDoge	A faster and stronger Doge that can dodge attacks. Appears in the [[Hatsune Miku Collaboration Event]].
MikuGory	A variant of Gory from the [[Hatsune Miku Collaboration Event]]. Has much higher stats and a chance to [[Special Abilities#Knockback|knockback]] cats.
MikuBear	A Teacher Bear variant exclusively appearing in the [[Hatsune Miku Collaboration Event]]. It has higher stats, but is Single Target.
Everlord Wanwan	The [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Alien]] variant of King Wahwah. He behaves very similarly, but has higher health and damage, and most of his damage distributed in the first two hits, with the third being weak while [[Special Abilities#Warp|warping]] units back by 2,000 range for over a minute.
Yakisoba Face	A variant of The Face that appears in the [[Nissin U.F.O. Collaboration Event]]. Has high range, one knockback, low movement speed and can [[warp]] Cat Units for 1,000 range.
Le'Grim	A [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] variant of Le'noir that appears in the [[Le'Grim Strikes]] [[Gauntlet]]. He has higher range and the ability to slow cats for 6.67 seconds. Though weak initially, he receives insane strength magnifications in the later stages of Le'Grim Strikes.
Death Angel Z-Onel	A [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant of Cli-One that has more health, damage and range, fewer knockbacks, near-instant unlimited [[Special Abilities#Revive|revives]] and can [[Special Abilities#Freeze|freeze]] Cats, but has a blind spot.
Li'l Zyclone	A [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] enemy that has high health and burrows far but has somewhat low DPS; its main role is to intercept the flow of meatshields. Unlike [[Zyclone]], it can only revive once. It appears in [[Into the Future]] Chapter 3 [[Zombie Outbreaks]] and [[Legend Stages#Uncanny Legends|Uncanny Legends]].
St. Dober	An [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angelic]] variant of Dober P.D. Has very high stats overall, with [[Surge Attack]]s instead of Waves and piercing Omni Strikes that extend his reach to 200.
Doremi	The [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] variant of Bakoo. Rather than freezing all of your Cat Units, Doremi only slows them down, but packs much higher stats than Bakoo.
Mega-Mooth	A [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] variant only found in [[Mega Menace]]. Similar to Othom, but stands at 370 and hits up to 470, and 100% chance to [[Special Abilities#Knockback|knockback]] cats that survive his attacks. Starts out weak, but receives massive buffs in later stages.
Koronium	A [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] variant of Kory. He only has a meager 150 health, but his high range and extreme damage remain threatening with his level 4 wave attacks.
Super Hyppoh	An Alien/[[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] variant of Hyppoh introduced in [[Horrorpotamus]]. She has a whopping 20 knockbacks, 100% chance to slow cats for 2 seconds, high damage, good health and despite her meager 222 standing range, has an Omni Strike that hits up to 350. Starts out weak, but receives massive buffs in later stages.
Zollow	A [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]]/[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] variant that has only one knockback, much less health, attack power and DPS. It does not [[Special Abilities#Burrow|burrow]], but comes with an Omni Strike extending his range, complete with Toxic attacks that deal 80% max health damage.
Evil Emperor Cat	The enemy version of [[Emperor Cat (Legend Rare Cat)|Emperor Cat]], a Nyandam-like [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] enemy found in the [[:Category:Advent Stages|Advent Stage]] [[Possessed by Evil (Merciless)|Prelude to Ruin]]. Deals relatively low damage but has an [[Special Abilities#Omni Strike|Omni Strike]] reaching up to 620 range, while also being able to do powerful [[Surge Attack]]s with both curse and freeze effects.
Cow Doge	A faster Doge that is essentially a stronger [[Rat Doge]]. Appears in the [[Gauntlet]] of the You Nears 2021 event, [[A Colossal New Year!]].
Bore Jr.	[[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] variant of Bore. Relatively fragile, but deals extremely high damage and creates Lv.5 [[Mini-Wave]]s with his attacks.
Chocolate Doge	Wall Doge's black variant designed to look like a chocolate bar. It can be found in certain [[Special Events|Event Stages]]. It possesses significantly more health and damage, with [[Special Abilities#Immune to Freeze|Freeze Immunity]] and a guaranteed chance to create Lv.4 [[Wave Attack#Mini-Wave|Mini-Waves]].
Ragin' Gory	A Black/[[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] variant of Gory Black, with more health, damage and range than Gory Black as well as immunity to freeze.
Aku Doge	An [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] variant of Doge, he has a weak [[Shield]] that regenerates with 50% HP for each damage-based knockback he takes.
Sinner Snache	An [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] variant of Snache. Deals high damage and has a 50% chance to create a Lv.1 [[Surge Attack|Surge]] upon death.
Cerberus Kids	An [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] variant of Those Guys. They have a chance to [[Special Abilities#Freeze|freeze]] units they hit for 4 seconds, but are still [[Special Abilities#Single Attack|Single Attack]] and have short range.
Condemned Peng	An [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] variant of Jackie Peng. He has much higher stats, higher range, Area Attack, a 50% chance to slow cat units and a guaranteed chance to create a Lv.3 [[Surge Attack]] upon death.
Aku Gory	Gory's [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] variant. Slower than Gory Black or Angelic Gory, but has even higher DPS, fewer knockbacks, and a chance to perform a [[Savage Blow]] which deals triple damage.
Le'Behemoth	An [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] variant of Le'Boin with blue skin, yellow eyes, black tusks, and a pentagram on his forehead. This variant is protected by a durable [[Shield]] and has only 380 range, but pushes more easily with an [[Special Abilities#Omni Strike|Omni Strike]] that reaches up to 410.
Fallen Bear	An [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] variant of Teacher Bear. His health and range are both subpar for his very high DPS, but he has a durable [[Shield]] and creates a Lv.1 [[Surge Attack]] upon death.
Wicked Face	An Aku variant of The Face. Has very long range with an even longer [[Mini-Wave]] attack, as well as freeze and a [[Shield]].
Aku Cyclone	Moves very slowly but has above average range, 4 knockbacks and a [[Shield]] with as much health as the Cyclone itself, 1,666,666, effectively giving it 8,333,330 HP. Topping this off is its [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] trait, leaving players with few reliable means of stalling it without [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cats]]. The only silver lining is that its damage per hit is relatively low compared to other Cyclones. It appears in [[Wrath of Hell (Deadly)|The Great Diablo]].
High Priest Mamon	A stronger variant of Dark Priest Mamon, with better stats, range, [[Shield]] and a [[Special Abilities#Toxic|Toxic]] effect that takes off 15% of Cat Units' maximum health.
Possessed Empress	The [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemy version of [[Princess Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Empress Cat]], with an extremely strong [[Shield]], piercing range and guaranteed [[Mini-Wave]]s and slow. Appears in [[Aku's Melody (Merciless)|Temptation's Symphony]].
Red Wind	White Wind's [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] variant. Has a higher movement speed, two more knockbacks and a 100% chance to [[Special Abilities#Weaken|weaken]] Cat Units to 50% for 1 second instead of knockback.
Black Wind	White Wind's [[:Category:Black Enemies|Black]] variant. Has 50% higher attack, 10 knockbacks and 12 movement speed, but has no special ability whatsoever.
Medu-san	An [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] variant of Mr. Mer that has lower overall stats and creates Lv.1 [[Surge Attack]]s instead of Mini-Waves.
Miz Devil	An Aku variant of Mr. Angel. Has shorter range to allow for easier pushing, has one knockback as opposed to eight, and most of her health comes in the form of a [[Shield]].
Sathankhamun VIII	An Aku variant of Hannya. Has slightly varied stats, but also has an Omni Strike and a 100% chance to slow every cat within its range.
Midnite D.	An [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] variant of Rain D. with high stats and a somewhat weak [[Shield]] that regenerates for each and every one of his 20 knockbacks.
Ackey	An [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] variant of Tackey. He has higher damage, slightly higher range, [[Special Abilities|multi-hit]] and a [[Shield]] that's much more durable than Ackey himself. Shoots a dodecahedron that causes three blasts, each having a 30% chance to [[Special Abilities#Freeze|freeze]] Cats for 2 seconds.
Deathkory	An [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] variant of Kory. He has a powerful [[Shield]] alongside an already-high health pool, in addition to firing level 6 Wave Attacks.
Masked Grandmaster Cat	A [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] variant of Hermit Cat that appears on [[Infernal Tower/Floor 30|Floor 30]] and [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 49|Floor 49]] of the [[Infernal Tower]]. Has the same amount of health, but deals even more damage and can curse every Cat Unit he hits.
Red EnerG	The [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] variant of H. Nah. He attacks and moves slightly slower, but has fewer knockbacks, higher range and 100% chance to additionally generate a level 2 [[Surge Attack]].
Archangel Exiel	A [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] variant of Mr. Angel that appears in the [[Divine Archangel Strikes]] gauntlet. He has amazing stats across the board as well as [[Special Abilities#Omni Strike|Omni Strike]], [[Special Abilities#Warp|Warp]], and [[Special Abilities#Weaken|Weaken]] abilities.
Big Peng Z	A [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] variant of Zackie Peng. Has surprisingly low attack power, but his attacks carry a 50% Toxic effect and an [[Special Abilities#Omni Strike|Omni Strike]] that reaches up to 500 range.
Tiger Doge	The same old New Year's Doge in a different costume. Appears in [[A Colossal New Year! (2021)]].
Nana & Doge	Chibi version of [[Kaohsiung Rapid Transit Collaboration Event|Kaohsiung Rapid Transit]] mascot Nana with a Doge by her side. Together they form a well-rounded enemy with piercing range and [[Mini-Wave]]s that can slow.
Emilia & Doge	Chibi version of Kaohsiung Rapid Transit mascot Emilia with a Doge by her side. Similar to Nana & Doge, but trades the Mini-Waves and slow for higher overall stats and a brief freeze effect.
Zapy	Capy's [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant has lower health, attack power, range and no [[Critical Hit]]s in exchange for a faster attack rate and plenty of other abilities such as [[Special Abilities#Warp|warp]], immunity to [[Wave Attack|waves]] and [[Surge Attack|surges]], and [[Special Abilities#Revive|reviving]].
Wild Doge	A [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]]/[[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] variant of Doge with much higher stats, shorter backswing and immunity to [[Surge Attack]]s. First appears in [[Empress' Excavation 1]].
Casaurian Ahirujo	A [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]/[[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] variant of Duche. Hits three times per attack instead of two, with much higher stats overall and some new abilities such as [[Special Abilities#Long Distance|Long Distance]] and a 5% chance to perform a [[Special Abilities#Savage Blow|Savage Blow]].
Pterowl Hazuku	A [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]]/[[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] variant that has three knockbacks instead of one, vastly superior stats overall besides speed and attack rate while also packing many new abilities like [[Special Abilities#Long Distance|Long Distance]], Surge Immunity and a 20% chance to create a Lv.1 [[Surge Attack]] within a wide spawn area.
Crustaceous Scissorex	An [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]]/[[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] variant of Helmut Krabbe with vastly higher damage, range and HP, a two-part [[Special Abilities#Long Distance|Long Distance]] attack that reaches further on the second hit, a 100% chance to [[Special Abilities#Slow|slow]] Cat Units and immunity to [[Wave Attack]]s. Does not have the ability to [[Special Abilities#Survive|survive]] a lethal strike.
J.J. Jackrabbit	A [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]/[[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] variant of B.B.Bunny with much higher stats overall, Area Attack, a chance to knockback cats, and a two-part attack with 100 piercing range on the second hit.
Li'l Doge	A miniature version of Doge. Has low stats but makes up for it with a 20% chance to dodge Cats' attacks for 1 second.
Golem Sunfish	A [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]]/[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] variant of Sunfish Jones. Similar to [[Ultima Beast Naala]], it has several dangerous abilities: [[Special Abilities#Freeze|freeze]], [[Special Abilities#Curse|curse]] and most notably, a 3-part [[Special Abilities#Multi-Hit|Multi-Hit]] [[Special Abilities#Long Distance|Long Distance]] attack with each attack striking a further area and getting weaker as it progresses.
THE FOLIVOREAN	An [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]]/[[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] variant of THE SLOTH with much higher stats, a weak [[Shield]], a [[Special Abilities#Multi-Hit|Multi-Hit]] attack that has different effective ranges, [[Special Abilities#Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]] and a 40% chance to [[Special Abilities#Freeze|freeze]] Cats for 3 seconds.
Casaurian Darkjo	A stronger Casaurian Ahirujo that is [[:Category:Black Enemies|Black]] instead of Red and trades Savage Blows for a 5% chance to do a Toxic attack which removes 50% of cats' HP.
Haniwanwan	A [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] enemy resembling [[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]]. Deals high amounts of Single Target damage from short range and creates Lv.4 Mini-Waves that can inflict knockback, freeze, slow, weaken, or curse.
Angelic Beast Rajakong	The toughest variant of Gory in terms of health, this Angel/Behemoth enemy's attacks have 50 piercing range and have a 10% chance to create a level 2 [[Wave Attack|Waves]]. He is also immune to Waves and [[Surge Attack|Surges]], but has a whopping 24 knockbacks.
Great Angel Chibinel	One of Cruel Angel Clionel's sons who separated from his mother, bolstered with the [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] attribute. Acts somewhat like an Angel/Colossus variant of [[Tackey]], with a blind spot of similar size and identical damage at 200%. Of course, the real challenge posed by this enemy is his 100% chance to slow and weaken cats for 3 seconds.
Spiritual Yulala	A [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] variant of Mystic Mask Yulala that appears on [[Infernal Tower/Floor 40|Floor 40]] and [[Infernal Tower/Floor 49|Floor 49]] of the [[Infernal Tower]]. Has significantly improved health and damage, can Curse and Warp every unit that survives the attack and has only 9 knockbacks instead of 10.
Osamu Mikumo & Doge	Chibi version of [[World Trigger Collaboration Event|World Trigger]] hero Osamu Mikumo with a Doge by his side. A slow, tanky enemy with high health and very low attack power and range, many immunities, Omni Strike with 50 piercing range and guaranteed Lv.3 Waves.
Yuma Kuga & Doge	Chibi version of World Trigger hero Yuma Kuga with a Doge by his side. A well-rounded melee enemy that constantly delivers Area Attacks with 100 piercing range and double damage upon reaching 50% HP.
Cumulus Gallus	A [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]]/[[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] variant of Chickful A, with much higher overall stats, shorter range, immunity to [[Special Abilities#Immune to Slow|Slow]] and [[Special Abilities#Immune to Weaken|Weaken]], and the ability to increase its own attack power by 150% at 33% HP.
Ancient Magamojoe	An even stronger Casaurian Ahirujo that's [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] instead of Red. Instead of a 5% chance for a Savage Blow, he has a 100% chance to [[Special Abilities#Curse|Curse]] and a 50% chance to create a level 2 [[Surge Attack]] on his third hit. He also trades Freeze immunity for Knockback immunity.
Zero Luza	A much stronger variant of Great Ape Luza that is a [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] enemy instead of a Behemoth, with better stats, range, freeze immunity and the ability to strengthen by 100% at 33% health.
Metafilibuster	A [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]]-only variant of Filibuster Obstructa with triple the damage, 1.5x health, and is additionally immune to [[Surge Attack]]s. Otherwise, he isn't much different from the original.
Rabbit Doge	The fourth entry in the costumed New Year's Doge series, dressed to the nines for [[A Colossal New Year! (2022)]] but no stronger than its predecessors - in fact, it has 5 less speed than Cow Doge and Tiger Doge.
Vermilingua Rangmaster	An [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]]/[[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] variant of Master A. He has a longer backswing and stands at 300 range, but his Omni Strikes hit up to 350. He's immune to [[Wave Attack|waves]] and knockback, with extreme health, damage and a resilient [[Shield]] that regenerates several times.
Devil Wife	An [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] variant of Celeboodle. She has slightly higher stats, but is often buffed. While remaining single-target, she always generates a Lv.1 [[Surge Attack]] upon death as a psuedo-Area Attack which can wipe out those not [[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|immune]].
Omens	A Colossus variant of Cerberus Kids introduced as the boss of [[Attack of the Omens]], with vastly improved stats, occasional [[Surge Attack|Surges]], and the ability to hit three times per attack.
Mini White Cyclone	The Li'l variant of [[White Cyclone|White Cyclone.]] He has a lot of health and powerful attacks, as well as only a single knockback. However, he has the standard Cyclone weakness of minuscule range, as well as being a [[Special Abilities#Single Attack|Single Attack]] attacker.
Infernal Pegasus Deonil	A [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] & [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] variant of Sleipnir. This hellish pegasus comes with a 100% chance to create a [[Wave Attack#Mini-Wave|Mini-Wave]], along with longer range and the ability to [[Special Abilities#Freeze|Freeze]] cats for almost 2 seconds.
Suidae Piggicus	[[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]]/[[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] variant of Pigge, with very high health and a 20% chance to freeze cat units for 2 seconds. Unlike Elizabeth the LVIth, it doesn't create [[Wave Attack]]s.
Elephantidae Papaou	A [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] variant of Le'Boin. Much stronger in health, damage and attack rate, has slightly longer range, and is immune to to all negative effects. However, he has half the movement speed and double the backswing of the original.
Infernal Tyrant Nyandam	A standing Aku variant of Nyandam without a throne. Though he stands at only 400 range, he has extreme health and an attack that deals 666k damage in an area of 400 range, then hits for 30% Toxic damage within ranges of 500~800 and 1,000~1,250. Additionally, he is immune to to weaken, knockback and Surge Attacks. Appears in all 4 stages of [[Reign of the Tyrant]].
Grand Mage Mimon	A [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemy found at the end of the [[Underground Labyrinth]]. Very similar to High Priest Mamon, but with even higher health and attack power, no Shield or Toxic ability and a 20% chance to slow units for 4 seconds.
Lutrinae Gokurakko	An [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] variant of Otta-smack-u with extremely magnified stats, 3 knockbacks, Omni Strikes that have a 50% chance to knock units back, and [[Counter-Surge]]. It still has a low cash drop for its difficulty.
Iguanidae Ibilujon	A [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]]/[[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] variant of Johnnyleon. It has more health, extreme damage, high range, an Omni Strike that reaches even further, a guaranteed 4-second curse, and the ability to replicate any [[Surge Attack|surges]] that hit it, on top of being immune to [[Wave Attack|waves]], knockback and weaken.
Lophiiformes Angaburu	A [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]], [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]], & [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] variant of Henry. He's a low-ranged support enemy with moderate health, high damage, 75% surge that can hit much further, and 100% chance to slow for 1.67 seconds.
Mega Baa Baa	Baa Baa's [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] variant, with an Omni Strike that adds 30 piercing range to the 200 it stands at, as well as the [[Counter-Surge]] ability. Hits much harder and up to three times per attack, but is still a single-target enemy.
Crocodylidae Kurocroc	The [[:Category:Black Enemies|Black]]/[[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] variant of Croco. Rather than being a peon, Kurocroc is a [[Mr. Puffington]]-like enemy with extremely high health and damage, an Omni Strike that extends their already high range a fair bit and a 100% chance to weaken Cat Units by 50% for 3 seconds. Their slower attack rate is balanced by a relatively long backswing. They boast immunity to slow and freeze on top of their high movement speed, though their 20 knockbacks make them easy to hold back until other threats enter play.
Mini Angel Cyclone	The Li'l variant of [[Divine Cyclone]]. She has a good amount of health and decent damage, with each hit being able to create a [[Surge Attack|Surge Attack]]. However, she suffers from an extremely short range and an outstanding 44 knockbacks.
King's Mimic	[[God (Special Cat)|Secret God]]'s Doge counterpart, created for the 11th anniversary event. A Floating backliner that deals almost no damage, but has very long reach and briefly freezes cats.
King Doge	Another 11th anniversary enemy. Looks like [[The Cat God]], but is actually just a weak Metal enemy used to give players easy rewards.
Esoteric Uril	A [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] variant of Master Uril that appears on [[Infernal Tower/Floor 50|Floor 50]] of the [[Infernal Tower]]. Gains 2 more knockbacks, but has higher health, attack power, range, Omni Strike reach and [[Surge Attack|Surge]] level and a 50% chance to slow units for 2 seconds.
Dragon Doge	The fifth New Year's Doge dons a dragon costume for [[A Colossal New Year! (2023)]]. Functions identically to Rabbit Doge.
Dogenstein	A [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]]/[[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] variant of Doge with extremely high health, Area Attack, fast movement speed, faster attack rate and a 35% chance to [[Special Abilities|Freeze]] your cats.
Tarsiriel	An [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]]/[[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] enemy similar to Loris, albeit with Slow instead of Curse, greater survivability, shorter range, and resistance to negative effects thanks to its Sage type.
Artillery Dummy	Has identical stats to a Dummy except a longer range of 450 and a significantly shorter attack frequency.
Dark Dober	A [[:Category:Black Enemies|Black]]/[[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] variant of Dober P.D. Deals less damage than St. Dober, but has a much further-reaching Omni Strike, extending up to 350 range. Creates [[Wave Attack|Mini-Wave]]s instead of normal Waves, along with Weakening Cats to 25%. It also has the most knockbacks among the Dobers, with 6.
Gigahaniwan	A [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]]/[[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] variant of Haniwanwan, with greatly improved overall stats, especially range, with the exception of lower damage. Its abilities now all have a 30% chance to be activated and last for 3 seconds, with the exception of [[Special Abilities#Curse|Curse]], which is now 100%. Its [[Wave Attack#Mini-Wave|Mini-Wave]] is replaced with a regular [[Wave Attack]], and it gains [[Special Abilities#Area Attack|Area Attack]] as well. To add onto this, it is also [[Special Abilities#Immune to Curse|Immune to Curse]] to prevent its abilities from being disabled. Starts out weak, but receives massive buffs in later stages.
Possessed King Doge	A more serious variant of King Doge created for the 11 and 1/2 anniversary event. Trading his [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] trait for [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]], Possessed King Doge is essentially a weaker version of [[The Cat God]] that briefly freezes units on each hit.
Doctor K.O.	Kang Roo's [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]/[[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] variant. Has similar stats to a 300% Shadow Boxer K, but with a higher money drop, health, range and speed and only 3 knockbacks.
Wave Dummy	A Dummy with level 20 [[Wave Attack]]s and a slightly longer attack frequency.
Techn-Old Hyena	This variant of H. Nah is a tanky [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Alien]]/[[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] enemy that warps cats back by 1,200 range for 16.67 seconds. Has fewer knockbacks, slightly longer range, [[Counter-Surge]], immunity to curse and Omni Strikes that extend his maximum reach to 390.
Diabrollow	An [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]]/[[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] variant that has lower attack power and DPS, but makes up for it with higher health,a greater Knockback count of 15, 100% chance to cause Knockback on whatever he hits and the ability to create a level 3 [[Mini-Wave]].
Oldstrich	The [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]]/[[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] variant of R.Ost. Unlike M. Ost, whose abilities and knockbacks often make him less of a threat than R.Ost, Oldstrich is practically a full upgrade, having 1.6M HP, 23k AP, 40.5k DPS, 300 range and infinite revives with none of M. Ost's drawbacks, on top of having 1 less knockback and higher speed than R.Ost. The 10% Critical chance is replaced with a 20% chance for a 20% [[Special Abilities#Toxic|Toxic]] attack.
Idi:Ne	A much weaker Idi:Re that has 1/6 as much health, half the attack power and no Strengthen ability, but is immune to [[Wave Attack|Waves]] and [[Surge Attack|Surges]]. After clearing [[Eldritch Forces/Invasion|Eldritch Forces Invasion]] and [[Revival of Origin]], she appears in [[The Face of God]], spawning countless times throughout its [[The Face of God/Invasion|Invasion stage]].
Bannerman Doge	A Doge turned into a foot soldier for the 12th anniversary. The hat, spear and banner do not grant any abilities nor stat improvements.
Commander Face	A helmeted Face introduced in 12th Anniversary stages, with higher health, speed and knockbacks than The Face.
Commander Nyandam	A Nyandam variant introduced in 12th Anniversary stages, with a 100% chance to knockback cats.
Commander Hannya	Another Red/Black variant of Hannya, introduced in the 12th Anniversary as opposed to an [[:Category:Advent Stages|Advent Stage]]. Similar to Hannya, but has lower health and attack power, attacks less frequently and trades Hannya's guaranteed 5-second weaken for a 30% chance of a 3-second freeze.
Commander Bun Bun	A Teacher Bun Bun variant introduced in 12th Anniversary stages. Has higher health and attack power and Omni Strikes that extend up to 280 range.
Snache Doge	The sixth New Year's Doge, dressed in a snake costume. Debuts in [[A Colossal New Year! (2024)]], functions identically to Dragon Doge and Rabbit Doge.
Mystery Snowmound	A snow-covered Razorback introduced in [[Snow Doges]]. Has one more frame of backswing compared to Razorback, but is otherwise identical.
Prof. Owlbrowley	A [[:Category:Black Enemies|Black]]/Floating/[[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] variant introduced in [[Zero Legends]]. Has higher health, damage, speed and range, but remains relatively frail and has a slightly slower attack rate. Their attack carries a 100% chance to freeze cats for 4 seconds and an [[Special Abilities#Omni Strike|Omni Strike]] with 440 maximum range.
Xenobeast Bunaglios	An Alien/[[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Boss]] introduced in the [[:Category:Advent Stages#Great Advent Stages|Great Advent Stage]] [[Hunt for the Xenobeast]]. Behaves rather differently from other Bun Buns, with a slower attack rate and animation, unusually long range (400 standing, 450 Omni Strike), a guaranteed [[Explosion]] that spawns at 400 range and a 20% [[Critical Hit|Critical]] chance. Surprisingly, Xenobeast Bunaglios is also '''not''' a Floating enemy.
Shachiko	A [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]]/[[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] variant of Dolphina. Has overall higher stats than Dolphina with higher range, but attack closer to them. Also guaranteed [[Special Abilities#Curse|Curse]] for 6s.
Holy Valkyrie Cat	A pure [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] variant of Corrupted Valkyrie that appears in [[Valkyrie Cat's Trial]]. She has more health, damage, speed and knockbacks, but her attack rate is much slower. Also strengthens at 50% HP instead of 40% and has a 75% chance to [[Special Abilities#Freeze|Freeze]] for 3s.
Awakened Bahamut Cat	A pure [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] variant of Raging Bahamut Cat that appears in [[Bahamut Cat's Trial]]. He has significantly more health, damage, speed and knockbacks in exchange for a longer time between attacks, longer backswing and shorter range. Also has a 100% chance to create an [[Explosion]] at 300 range on his 1st hit.
Perry Duche	A pure Black variant of Duche that lacks multi-hit, but has guaranteed [[Explosion]]s, medium range and piercing Omni Strikes.
Puffzerker	A less powerful [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] variant of Mr. Puffington that weakens units to 25% instead of Cursing them.
Commander Ostromeda	The [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] variant of R.Ost. Similar to a 200% R. Ost in terms of base stats, with 290 range. Despite not being a [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Alien]], they have a 15% chance to [[warp]] cats back by 800 range for 6.7 seconds.
Ange Lackey	An [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]]/[[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] variant of Tackey. They have the highest health among Tackey's variants, a 50% chance to knockback cats, guaranteed [[Explosion]]s, and the range to mess with most expensive backliners (600 standing range, 450~750 effective range).
South Seas Doge	A Traitless variant of Doge with 2x the health and 3x the damage. It also has a chance to knockback Cats and Survive lethal strikes, but is otherwise still entirely unnoteworthy.
South Seas Otter	An Otta-smack-u variant from [[Island Defenders!]]. Guaranteed to slow units for 3 seconds and has 300 range, 3 knockbacks and a 30% chance to create a level 3 [[Mini-Surge]] at 300~500.
Freeze Dummy	Its damage is much weaker, but it has a lengthy range of 800, attacks that are about twice more frequent, and a guaranteed 5 second [[Special Abilities#Freeze|Freeze]].
Whiskingmeister	A seasonal Traitless enemy that has higher health, slightly lower speed and a 30% chance to knockback units, but is otherwise very similar to Kory.
Fireworks Gang	A bigger trio of stick figures, though not as large as Omens. They have very high health and DPS for a Those Guys variant, attack as fast as a [[Cyclone]] and have surprisingly long reach, with 250 range, 400 Omni Strike and a 20% chance to create a level 1 Surge at 150~650.
Jumbo Jones	An [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]]/[[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] variant of Sunfish Jones introduced in the [[:Category:Advent Stages#Great Advent Stages|Great Advent Stage]] [[Jumbo Invasion]]. He only has 450 range and his knockback count is increased to 5, but he hits twice per attack (20k at -300~450 on 1st hit, 90k with a level 7 [[Wave Attack|Wave]] and 2-second slow at 451~751 on 2nd hit), is immune to freeze and weaken, and moves very fast for a Great [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Boss]], with 35 speed.
Deathshund	A [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant from [[Zero Legends]]. Has even longer range than Lucky Dags and a burrow distance of 900, revives once with 100% HP and freezes cats for 2 seconds, but doesn't attack as frequently as other Dagshund variants.
Supervillain Doge	?
Evilzabeth	[[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]]/[[:Category:Supervillain Enemies|Supervillain]] variant of Pigge, with a far higher attack rate, DPS and health, but only a single knockback. It also has a 30% chance to generate a level 2 Mini-Wave, as well as a Shield.
Face Baron	A [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]/[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]]/[[:Category:Supervillain Enemies|Supervillain]] variant of Shy Boy.
Big Face Baron	A visually larger variant of Face Baron with stronger health and attack stats, more range, and longer attack cycles and animations.